T.A.P. Frontend File Guide
Derrick Ellis

index.html
- Main login page for the Tiger Attendance Portal.
- Allows users to enter login information.
- Lets the user choose whether they are a Student or Instructor.

script.js
- Handles the login page behavior.
- Reads the selected role.
- Directs the user to the correct dashboard.

student.html
- Contains the layout for the student dashboard.
- Includes course selection, session selection, webcam area, check-in button, and status messages.

student.js
- Controls student dashboard functionality.
- Loads course and session information.
- Accesses the webcam.
- Captures an image for attendance verification.
- Sends the check-in request to the backend API.
- Displays success or error messages.

instructor.html
- Contains the layout for the instructor dashboard.
- Includes session creation, student roster, search, attendance records, and dashboard statistics.

instructor.js
- Handles instructor dashboard functionality.
- Loads courses from the backend API.
- Creates new class sessions.
- Validates session information.
- Loads class sessions.
- Handles student roster search.
- Connects instructor actions to the backend.

style.css
- Controls the visual design of the frontend.
- Includes the maroon T.A.P. theme.
- Styles login pages, dashboards, forms, buttons, cards, tables, status badges, and responsive layouts.

Frontend Summary
- The frontend was built using HTML, CSS, and JavaScript.
- It provides separate interfaces for students and instructors.
- It connects to the backend API for course, session, and attendance-related functions.
- Some data may still use mock information while full backend and face-recognition integration is completed.
